<title>AUSTRIA: TENNIS-GENERALI OPEN MEN'S TOURNAMENT RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-GENERALI OPEN MEN'S TOURNAMENT RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KITZBUEHEL, Austria 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from</p>
<p>$535,000 Generali Open men's tennis tournament on Tuesday</p>
<p>(prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p>Stefan Koubek (Austria) beat David Rikl (Czech Republic) 2-6</p>
<p>6-1 7-5</p>
<p>Marcos Aurelio Gorriz (Spain) beat Sebastian Prieto (Argentina)</p>
<p>6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Bernd Karbacher (Germany) beat Jaime Oncins (Brazil) 7-6 (7-3)</p>
<p>6-2</p>
<p>Carlos Costa (Spain) beat Emilio Alvarez (Spain) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Lucas Arnold (Argentina) beat Daniel Orsanic (Argentina) 6-1</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Julian Alonso (Spain) beat Markus Hipf (Austria) 7-5 4-6 6-1</p>
<p>Nicolas Lapentti (Ecuador) beat Emilio Sanchez (Spain) 2-6 6-1</p>
<p>6-1</p>
<p>Gerald Mandl (Austria) beat Gilbert Schaller (Austria) 5-2</p>
<p>(Schaller retired injured)</p>
<p>8-Juan Albert Viloca (Spain) beat Oleg Ogorodov (Uzbekistan)</p>
<p>6-2 6-0</p>
<p>Martin Sinner (Germany) beat Werner Eschauer (Austria) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Second Round</p>
<p>15-Slava Dosedel (Czech Republic) beat Thierry Champion</p>
<p>(France) 6-3 6-2</p>
</text>
